---
import { COMPOSE_URL, CONFIG_TABS, INFRASTRUCTURE_DOC_URL } from '@lib/solutions/self-hosting';
---

<section class="border-t border-line bg-app" aria-labelledby="sh-config-title">
  <div class="wrap py-16 md:py-24 grid lg:grid-cols-12 gap-10 lg:gap-12">
    <div class="lg:col-span-5">
      <h2 id="sh-config-title" class="h2">
        What the repository gives you today.
      </h2>
      <p class="prose mt-5 max-w-[46ch]">
        <a class="link" href={COMPOSE_URL}>
          docker-compose.yml
        </a>{' '}
        starts the data tier: PostgreSQL 16, Redis 7 and RustFS as the S3-compatible store, with development
        credentials. It does not run the web app or the API, and it is not a production install.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm">
        <a class="link" href={INFRASTRUCTURE_DOC_URL}>
          Every variable and what it does
          <span class="arr ext" aria-hidden="true">
            ↗
          </span>
        </a>
      </p>

      <div class="rule-list mt-8">
        <div class="py-5">
          <h3 class="h3">A long-running API.</h3>
          <p class="prose mt-2 text-base">
            Not serverless. The job queue holds a Postgres connection and runs scheduled work inside the API process.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="py-5">
          <h3 class="h3">Web and API on one domain.</h3>
          <p class="prose mt-2 text-base">
            Sharing a registrable domain is what lets the session cookie stay <code>SameSite=Lax</code>. Set{' '}
            <code>SESSION_COOKIE_DOMAIN</code> to cover both.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="py-5">
          <h3 class="h3">A separate application role.</h3>
          <p class="prose mt-2 text-base">
            Create <code>nothingleft_app</code> before the first migration. The owner migrates; the application role
            runs queries and cannot rewrite the audit log.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="py-5">
          <h3 class="h3">Checked at boot.</h3>
          <p class="prose mt-2 text-base">
            Every variable is validated when the API starts. A bad configuration stops it starting, rather than failing
            on the first request.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="lg:col-span-7">
      <div class="tabs" data-tabs>
        <div class="tablist" role="tablist" aria-label="Configuration file">
          {CONFIG_TABS.map((tab, index) => (
            <button
              type="button"
              role="tab"
              id={`sh-tab-${tab.id}`}
              aria-controls={`sh-panel-${tab.id}`}
              aria-selected={index === 0 ? 'true' : 'false'}
              tabindex={index === 0 ? 0 : -1}
            >
              {tab.name}
            </button>
          ))}
        </div>
        {CONFIG_TABS.map((tab, index) => (
          <div
            class:list={['tabpanel', { on: index === 0 }]}
            role="tabpanel"
            id={`sh-panel-${tab.id}`}
            aria-labelledby={`sh-tab-${tab.id}`}
          >
            <div class="tabpanel-bar">
              <span class="tab-title text-sm font-medium text-fg mono">{tab.name}</span>
              <span class="text-xs text-fg-2">{tab.where}</span>
              <button type="button" class="copy" data-copy={`sh-config-${tab.id}`}>
                Copy
              </button>
            </div>
            <pre
              id={`sh-config-${tab.id}`}
              class="config sh-config"
              tabindex="0"
              aria-label={`${tab.name}, ${tab.where}`}
              set:html={tab.html}
            />
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-fg-2">
        Placeholders in capitals and <code class="mono">example.com</code> addresses stand in for yours. Never commit
        real values.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .sh-config {
    max-height: 760px;
    overflow: auto;
  }
  .sh-config :global(.c) {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }
  .sh-config :global(.k) {
    font-weight: 500;
  }
</style>
